<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FBType Name="AD_TO_AR_NUM" Comment="Composite FB for numerically converting AD (DWORD) adapter to AR (REAL) adapter&#10;(via UDINT, not a bit-reinterpretation)">
	<Identification Standard="61499-2" Description="Copyright (c) 2026 HR Agrartechnik GmbH  &#10; &#10;This program and the accompanying materials are made  &#10;available under the terms of the Eclipse Public License 2.0  &#10;which is available at https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/  &#10; &#10;SPDX-License-Identifier: EPL-2.0">
	</Identification>
	<VersionInfo Organization="HR Agrartechnik GmbH" Version="1.0" Author="Franz Höpfinger" Date="2026-08-30">
	</VersionInfo>
	<CompilerInfo packageName="adapter::conversion::unidirectional">
	</CompilerInfo>
	<InterfaceList>
		<Plugs>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="AR_OUT" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AR" Comment="REAL Adapter Output" x="2400" y="0"/>
		</Plugs>
		<Sockets>
			<AdapterDeclaration Name="AD_IN" Type="adapter::types::unidirectional::AD" Comment="DWORD Adapter Input" x="-800" y="0"/>
		</Sockets>
	</InterfaceList>
	<FBNetwork>
		<FB Name="ToUDINT" Type="iec61131::conversion::F_DWORD_TO_UDINT" x="-100" y="0">
		</FB>
		<FB Name="ToREAL" Type="iec61131::conversion::F_UDINT_TO_REAL" x="1100" y="0">
		</FB>
		<EventConnections>
			<Connection Source="AD_IN.E1" Destination="ToUDINT.REQ"/>
			<Connection Source="ToUDINT.CNF" Destination="ToREAL.REQ"/>
			<Connection Source="ToREAL.CNF" Destination="AR_OUT.E1"/>
		</EventConnections>
		<DataConnections>
			<Connection Source="AD_IN.D1" Destination="ToUDINT.IN"/>
			<Connection Source="ToUDINT.OUT" Destination="ToREAL.IN"/>
			<Connection Source="ToREAL.OUT" Destination="AR_OUT.D1"/>
		</DataConnections>
	</FBNetwork>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>AD_TO_AR_NUM</h1>

<h2>🇩🇪 Deutsch</h2>

<p>Numerisch korrekte Alternative zu <code>AD_TO_AR</code>. Wandelt einen DWORD-Adapter (<code>AD_IN</code>) über einen internen UDINT-Zwischenschritt in einen REAL-Adapter (<code>AR_OUT</code>) um — <strong>echte Wertumwandlung</strong>, keine Bit-Reinterpretation.</p>

<h3>Warum nicht einfach AD_TO_AR?</h3>

<p><code>AD_TO_AR</code> nutzt intern <code>F_DWORD_TO_REAL</code>, was im FORTE-Kern für Bit-String-Typen (DWORD/WORD/BYTE/LWORD) eine reine IEEE754-Bit-Reinterpretation ist, keinen numerischen Cast. Ein roher Zähler-/Analogwert wie <code>DWORD#2048</code> würde dadurch NICHT zu <code>REAL#2048.0</code>, sondern zu einer bedeutungslosen Zahl nahe Null.</p>

<p><code>AD_TO_AR_NUM</code> vermeidet diese Falle, indem es zweistufig über <code>F_DWORD_TO_UDINT</code> (Bit-Reinterpretation DWORD→UDINT, hier gültig, da beide dieselbe 32-bit-Darstellung eines vorzeichenlosen Integers teilen) und anschließend <code>F_UDINT_TO_REAL</code> (echter numerischer Cast) konvertiert — dieselbe Kette, die bereits in mehreren Übungen (<code>Uebung_028a_AR</code> u.a.) von Hand verdrahtet wird, hier als ein einziger, drop-in-kompatibler Baustein.</p>

<h3>Wann welchen Baustein verwenden?</h3>

<ul>
	<li><strong>AD_TO_AR_NUM</strong>: Der DWORD-Wert ist eine Zahl (z. B. Analog-Rohwert, Zähler) und soll als derselbe Zahlenwert in REAL vorliegen.</li>
	<li><strong>AD_TO_AR</strong>: Der DWORD-Wert ist bereits ein Bitmuster, das als REAL interpretiert werden soll (z. B. Ergebnis von <code>F_REAL_TO_DWORD</code>, seriellisierte Float-Daten).</li>
</ul>

<h2>🇬🇧 English</h2>

<p>Numerically correct alternative to <code>AD_TO_AR</code>. Converts a DWORD adapter (<code>AD_IN</code>) into a REAL adapter (<code>AR_OUT</code>) via an internal UDINT step — a <strong>real value conversion</strong>, not a bit-reinterpretation.</p>

<h3>Why not just use AD_TO_AR?</h3>

<p><code>AD_TO_AR</code> internally uses <code>F_DWORD_TO_REAL</code>, which in the FORTE core is a pure IEEE754 bit-reinterpretation for bit-string types (DWORD/WORD/BYTE/LWORD), not a numeric cast. A raw counter/analog value such as <code>DWORD#2048</code> would NOT become <code>REAL#2048.0</code> but a meaningless value near zero.</p>

<p><code>AD_TO_AR_NUM</code> avoids this trap by converting in two steps via <code>F_DWORD_TO_UDINT</code> (bit-reinterpretation DWORD→UDINT, valid here since both share the same 32-bit unsigned-integer representation) and then <code>F_UDINT_TO_REAL</code> (a real numeric cast) — the same chain already wired by hand in several exercises (<code>Uebung_028a_AR</code> and others), packaged here as a single drop-in-compatible block.</p>

<h3>Which block to use?</h3>

<ul>
	<li><strong>AD_TO_AR_NUM</strong>: The DWORD value is a number (e.g. raw analog value, counter) and should carry the same numeric value as REAL.</li>
	<li><strong>AD_TO_AR</strong>: The DWORD value is already a bit pattern meant to be interpreted as REAL (e.g. the result of <code>F_REAL_TO_DWORD</code>, serialized float data).</li>
</ul>
]]></Attribute>
</FBType>
